Logic inherited the structure of theology. The parallels are not metaphorical—they are structural:

| Property | Theology (God) | Philosophy (Logic) |
|----------|---------------|-------------------|
| Self-grounding | Ens a se | Self-justifying axioms |
| Unconditioned | Not dependent on anything | Not dependent on experience |
| Absolute certainty | Perfect knowledge | Deductive certainty |
