This was the **declaration of independence**. Logic said:

> "I am the ground."
> "I am self-justifying."
> "I am complete."
> "I am the answer."
> "I am the truth."
> "I need no God."

### 3.2 The Claim of Self-Grounding

The claim of self-grounding took the form:

```
∀L (Logic(L) → SelfGround(L))
```

This claim meant:
- Logic does not depend on anything outside itself
- Logic can prove its own consistency
- Logic can justify its own axioms
